From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 03:31:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 14/15] browser: expose payload-free mutation phase
 observations

Add an opt-in observer for mutation enqueue, possible send, response,
covering reactive transition, retry, and promise settlement phases.
Preserve logical mutation identity across write-conflict retries while
retaining per-attempt request IDs for timing correlation.

Keep the observer outside transport ordering and mutation authority.
Disable failed observers and bound retry bookkeeping without changing
request retry, completion, or pressure behavior. Do not expose arguments,
results, credentials, log lines, or error text.

Validated with mutation tracing and client behavior tests, SDK build,
type checks, and generated runtime/declaration/source-map correspondence.
